<title>USA: Brent crude edges up in light U.S. paper trading.</title>
<headline>Brent crude edges up in light U.S. paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent crude oil edged up in light U.S. paper trading on Wednesday, traders said.</p>
<p>Four partial cargoes of August Brent changed hands at $18.22, $18.24, $18.28 and $18.32 a barrel.</p>
<p>August Brent was last pegged at $18.22-30 a barrel, up from the IPE settlement of $18.22.</p>
<p>July/August Brent was at plus 25-35 cents, while August/September was at minus 10/8 cents. September/October was at minus 15/13 cents.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
